// `lower` publishes only `result <= value`, but its checked body returns its
// argument, and the caller's `ensures` reads `lower(value)` denotationally:
// the invocation is checked, observation-free, reach-free, crash-free and
// terminating (wiki/spec/proofs/contracts.md), and mathematical conversion
// unfolds checked definitions (wiki/spec/proofs/mathematical_bindings.md), so
// the equality holds. The twin
// fail/core/scoped_integer_call_crash_route_blocks_unfolding gives `lower` a
// crash route.
machine lower(value: i16) -> i16 ensures result <= value { value }
machine caller(value: i16) -> i16
ensures (lower(value) as i16 in Saturating) == result { value }
machine main() {}
